    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Now, consider the elements a , x 1 , x 2 ∈ L . a ∧ x 1 ∧ x 2 ≠ 0 because otherwise we would have x 1 ∧ x 2 ⩽ b , as b is a pseudo-complement of a . Moreover c ∧ x k ≠ 0 for each k , because otherwise we would have c ∧ x k ⩽ b . Finally c ∧ a ≠ 0 , because otherwise c ⩽ b , contradicting our assumption. As c is a µ -element in L , we conclude that c ∧ a ∧ x 1 ∧ x 2 ≠ 0 , which proves the claim."
