    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Remark 3.16 . An analogue of part (2) of Proposition 3.15 does not hold for upsets. Consider the frame of power set P( X ) of the set X = { 1 , 2 , 3 , 4 , 5 } . We have { 1 , 2 }↝ µ { 1 } ↑ and { 3 , 4 }↝ µ { 3 } ↑ , by Remark 3.12 . However, it is easy to see that { 1 , 2 }∨{ 3 , 4 } = { 1 , 2 , 3 , 4 } is not a µ -element in { 1 , 3 } ↑ = { 1 }∨{ 3 } ↑ . Moreover, it is also not a µ -element in P( X ) ."
  }, {
